/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:10:#     - the only arrow shape is still a 3-pixel L inside a 2x2 box
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:12:#     - walls are still monochrome size-1 or size-3 axis-aligned segments
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:13:#     - wall color is still inherited by the propagation after a hit
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:15:#     - original: each arrow owns one ray that keeps bouncing through multiple walls
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:16:#     - variant: only one initial arrow is generated; when a ray touches a wall, that
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:17:#       ray stops there and the hit wall becomes the new source
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:18:#     - for a size-3 wall, all three wall pixels emit parallel child rays in the
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:19:#       reflected direction, so the propagation visibly fans out
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:21:#     - the arrow still fires from its right-angle vertex away from the missing corner
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:22:#     - a corner hit into a wall cell spawns a child source from that wall with
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:24:#     - a side-touch hit from ray cell (r,c) into a wall adjacent on the row side
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:25:#       flips dr and activates that wall as the new source
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:26:#     - a side-touch hit into a wall adjacent on the column side flips dc and
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:27:#       activates that wall as the new source
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:28:#     - on a hit, the last painted bounce cell takes the wall's color, matching the
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:29:#       original "adopt wall color at the interaction point" cue
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:31:#     - original flow: arrow ray walks NE, touches a horizontal wall, flips vertical
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:32:#       direction, continues itself, later touches another wall, and so on
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:33:#     - variant flow: arrow ray walks NE, touches the same horizontal wall, stops,
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:34:#       recolors the bounce cell, and the wall's pixels now emit new rays NW
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:35:#     - difference: later painted cells no longer belong to one continuously bounced
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:38:#     - generator always uses exactly one initial arrow to make the "chain reaction"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:40:#     - at least one activated wall is size 3, so the new source is visibly a wall
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:42:#     - chain length is 2-4 wall activations: enough for multi-step reasoning, small
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:45:#     - original loop assumed every arrow can be solved independently; that no longer
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:50:#     - original wall_cells was only a blocker set; now each wall component must keep
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:51:#       its full pixel list because the whole wall acts as the spawned source
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:52:#     - original overlap safety relied on independent arrows and never had to guard
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:53:#       against processing the same wall repeatedly; now main keeps an activated set
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:54:#       keyed by wall id and direction
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:57:#       activated size-3 wall emits parallel side rays that simply exit the board
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:58:#     - after a ray is committed, generator records "future wall forbidden" cells
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:59:#       beside that ray, so no later wall can retroactively create an earlier hit
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:60:#     - rays, arrows, and walls never share cells; walls are also kept away from
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:63:#     - the input contains one arrow but multiple isolated walls; the output shows
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:65:#       wall activates
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:67:#       arrow contributes one thin zigzag trajectory
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:69:#     - every non-arrow component is a legal wall segment of size 1 or 3
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/1/code.py:70:#     - repeated activation of the same wall-direction pair is not needed; generator
