/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D16/1/code.py:39:#     - if wall color = 2: dr does not flip, (r,c) stays 2, path continues straight.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D16/1/code.py:40:#     - if wall color = 5: dr flips to -dr, (r,c) becomes 5, later path continues in 5.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D16/1/code.py:46:# - This avoids a degenerate regime where every wall happens to be different-colored,
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D16/1/code.py:50:# - Original corner-hit block assumed every wall cell is an impenetrable blocker.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D16/1/code.py:52:# - Original side-touch blocks unconditionally flipped dr/dc when a wall was present.
