/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/1/code.py:3:# Change: color_change_on_bounce——射线在每次反射时采用墙壁的颜色，反射点也被重新涂为墙壁颜色... → 保持初始颜色不变
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/1/code.py:16:#    Objects stay the same as the original task: 3-cell L-shaped arrows plus 1-cell or 3-cell walls.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/1/code.py:17:#    The only semantic change is the ray color after a bounce. Originally, if a red ray touched a grey wall,
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/1/code.py:18:#    the bounce cell was recolored grey and all later ray cells also became grey. In this variant, that same
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/1/code.py:19:#    ray still reflects at the same location and with the same direction flip, but every ray cell before and
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/1/code.py:20:#    after the bounce remains red. The wall color is now only a reflector marker, not a paint source.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/1/code.py:21:#    Example: arrow color 2, vertical wall color 5 adjacent to bounce cell.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/1/code.py:22:#    Original: ... 2, 2, [bounce becomes 5], then later cells 5, 5, 5 ...
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/1/code.py:23:#    Variant : ... 2, 2, [bounce stays 2],  then later cells 2, 2, 2 ...
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/1/code.py:24:#    Therefore the changed stage is "bounce handling" in both solver and output-first generator.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/1/code.py:26:#    If we allowed all arrows to have zero bounces, the sample could look identical to the original task and the
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/1/code.py:27:#    D4 change would be invisible. The generator therefore ensures at least one bounced ray per sample. To make
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/1/code.py:28:#    the invariant-color rule visually obvious, wall colors are sampled from colors not used by arrows, so the
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/1/code.py:29:#    human sees repeated cases where a differently colored wall reflects the ray without recoloring it.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/1/code.py:31:#    - `cur_col` changed on each bounce. That no longer holds; ray color must stay equal to the arrow color.
