/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/1/code.py:37:#    Generator still enforces in-bounds arrow boxes, diagonal ray paths, non-overlap with prior objects, and
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/1/code.py:38:#    valid 1-cell-off wall placement. Additionally it tracks planned wall cells during a single arrow trace so
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/1/code.py:39:#    later segments cannot accidentally step onto an earlier wall and create an unintended corner bounce.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/1/code.py:41:#    Every generated sample contains at least one bounce, and bounced rays keep crossing beside walls whose color
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/1/code.py:42:#    differs from the ray color. Across 2-4 examples this should make the new rule legible: walls redirect rays
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/1/code.py:45:#    Rays, arrows, and walls remain disjoint. Wall colors are reused from a small wall-only pool, which keeps
