/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D7/3/code.py:3:# Change: 单像素或3像素轴对齐线段墙壁，放置在射线对角线路径旁偏移1格的位置... → 移动墙壁（墙壁在反射后消失）
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D7/3/code.py:21:#       - walls are still monochrome connected components, either size 1 or a 3-pixel axis-aligned segment
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D7/3/code.py:22:#       - walls still sit one orthogonal cell off a diagonal ray and trigger the same reflection geometry
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D7/3/code.py:24:#       - a wall is no longer static scenery
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D7/3/code.py:25:#       - once any ray uses a wall for reflection, the entire connected wall component disappears immediately
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D7/3/code.py:26:#       - disappeared wall cells become background-like: later rays may pass through and paint those cells
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D7/3/code.py:28:#     - state now matters, so arrows are processed in row-major order of their right-angle launch cell
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D7/3/code.py:29:#     - generator only creates one intentionally shared wall, and the earlier arrow is placed above/left of the later arrow
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D7/3/code.py:31:#     - outputs remove used walls
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D7/3/code.py:32:#     - at least one later ray passes through a wall cell that existed in the input, so the disappearance is functional, not cosmetic
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D7/3/code.py:36:#     - arrow A bounces off wall W, but W stays in place forever
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D7/3/code.py:37:#     - if arrow B later reaches W, it still bounces or stops there
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D7/3/code.py:39:#     - arrow A bounces off W and W is erased immediately
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D7/3/code.py:40:#     - arrow B later reaches the same cell and treats it as empty space, painting through it
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D7/3/code.py:43:#     - A reaches bounce cell (8,7), sees side wall at (8,8), flips dc and W disappears
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D7/3/code.py:47:#   - I keep the original arrow shape and side-bounce geometry intact.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D7/3/code.py:48:#   - I do not introduce moving directions or multi-step wall motion; "erase after one use" is the minimal stateful D7 change.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D7/3/code.py:49:#   - To avoid the variant becoming too weak, every generated instance contains one shared wall that is both consumed and later traversed.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D7/3/code.py:52:#   - Original `wall_cells` was immutable. That breaks here; I replace it with mutable wall-component ownership.
